WEBVTT

00:00.511 --> 00:03.362
♪ It seems today that all you see ♪

00:03.395 --> 00:06.766
♪ Is violence in
movies and sex on TV ♪

00:06.799 --> 00:10.469
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:10.502 --> 00:13.472
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:13.505 --> 00:16.844
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:16.877 --> 00:20.179
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:20.212 --> 00:22.045
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:22.046 --> 00:23.115
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:23.148 --> 00:28.588
♪ He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:33.359 --> 00:35.962
We now return to the extended
director's cut

00:35.996 --> 00:38.699
of Willy Wonka and the
Chocolate Factory.

00:38.731 --> 00:42.235
♪ ♪

00:42.268 --> 00:44.972
Charlie, don't forget
what happened to the boy

00:45.005 --> 00:47.341
- who got everything he ever wanted.
- What?

00:47.373 --> 00:49.075
He lived happily ever after.

00:49.108 --> 00:51.010
But he did have to earn it.

00:51.043 --> 00:52.179
Hint, hint.

00:52.212 --> 00:53.412
Do it, Charlie!

00:53.445 --> 00:55.915
I'm not going back
to that four-person bed!

00:55.948 --> 00:57.817
Hell, I'll do it, if you want!

00:57.850 --> 00:59.486
No! It has to be a child!

00:59.519 --> 01:01.088
What did he just say?

01:01.120 --> 01:02.655
Brian, this does not seem appropriate

01:02.689 --> 01:04.091
to watch in front of the baby.

01:04.123 --> 01:05.524
Not appropriate?

01:05.558 --> 01:08.295
You took me to see Magic Mike XXL.

01:09.261 --> 01:11.064
Uhp, this one's wet.

01:11.096 --> 01:12.899
Uh, this one, too.

01:12.933 --> 01:14.501
Also wet.

01:14.534 --> 01:16.270
Huh. This one's dry,

01:16.302 --> 01:18.838
but the back of the
seat in front of it is wet.

01:18.871 --> 01:22.376
Let's put on
something more child-friendly.

01:22.409 --> 01:25.545
Time to "Too-tooty-too"
with The Turtlenecks!

01:25.578 --> 01:28.215
Oh, God, no. These guys are horrible.

01:29.316 --> 01:30.716
♪ Do you kazoo? ♪

01:30.749 --> 01:32.218
♪ I often do ♪

01:32.251 --> 01:34.086
♪ When I am blue ♪

01:34.120 --> 01:35.522
♪ I do kazoo ♪

01:35.555 --> 01:37.224
♪ Tootooty-Too ♪

01:37.257 --> 01:38.859
♪ Goes my kazoo ♪

01:38.891 --> 01:40.593
♪ I will kazoo ♪

01:40.626 --> 01:42.295
♪ Hey how 'bout you? ♪

01:42.329 --> 01:43.805
Uch. All they're doing

01:43.829 --> 01:45.373
is announcing that they play the kazoo,

01:45.397 --> 01:47.867
and then asking if others
also play the kazoo.

01:47.900 --> 01:49.435
This doesn't seem so bad.

01:49.468 --> 01:51.237
I mean, after all,
it's a song for babies.

01:51.270 --> 01:52.710
Yeah, but-but that's the thing.

01:52.863 --> 01:55.608
Baby songs never tackle
real baby issues.

01:55.642 --> 01:57.644
You know, like... like loud noises.

01:57.645 --> 01:58.543
Or teething.

01:58.544 --> 02:00.814
Or when Dad uses me as a lumbar pillow.

02:00.846 --> 02:02.381
- Eh...
- Ow.

02:02.415 --> 02:04.051
- Eh...
- Ow. Ow.

02:04.083 --> 02:05.152
Ow.

02:05.184 --> 02:06.285
Ow.

02:06.319 --> 02:08.922
This thing works better in the car.

02:08.954 --> 02:10.589
Well, how could they
address baby issues?

02:10.623 --> 02:12.492
Children's songs are written by adults.

02:12.524 --> 02:15.295
And, dollars to donuts, white adults.

02:15.327 --> 02:17.684
I-I.. Who-who are
you mad at, Brian?

02:17.684 --> 02:18.874
Uch, how much time you got?

02:18.908 --> 02:20.184
Not enough for that, but you're right.

02:20.208 --> 02:21.843
If you want a song a baby'll like,

02:21.876 --> 02:23.413
you've got to get a baby to write it.

02:23.445 --> 02:24.846
Well, call John Mayer.

02:24.880 --> 02:25.815
He's a big, fat baby.

02:25.848 --> 02:27.717
No, I'll do it, and you can help.

02:27.749 --> 02:28.818
Well, I... I did write

02:28.850 --> 02:30.819
a musical about Alexander Hamilton.

02:30.852 --> 02:31.830
Not-not that one,

02:31.854 --> 02:33.155
but, uh, sure, I'm in.

02:33.189 --> 02:34.157
Ooh, I'm excited.

02:34.189 --> 02:35.257
This'll be great.

02:35.290 --> 02:37.759
And those guys back at
the factory can suck it.

02:37.792 --> 02:39.661
I'm gonna get out of this place one day.

02:39.695 --> 02:40.697
Hey, Butch.

02:40.730 --> 02:41.863
Get a load of Stewie.

02:41.897 --> 02:43.600
He says he's gonna get out of here.

02:45.201 --> 02:46.836
You don't know me, man. I'm different.

02:46.868 --> 02:47.869
I got ideas.

02:47.903 --> 02:49.706
Hey, Butch, you hear that?

02:49.738 --> 02:50.839
Stewie's got ideas.

02:50.873 --> 02:51.840
Shut up!

02:51.874 --> 02:53.276
I'm gonna go across that river

02:53.308 --> 02:55.177
and make it to the city
on the other side.

02:55.211 --> 02:56.612
I'm gonna be a singer.

02:56.646 --> 02:58.947
Bubl├й over here says
he's gonna be a singer.

02:58.981 --> 03:01.117
Hey, Bubl├й, I got a
tune for you to sing.

03:01.149 --> 03:05.288
It's called "Get Your Ass Back
on the Forklift, Lunch is Over".

03:05.320 --> 03:08.390
Hey, Stewie, don't listen to those guys.

03:08.423 --> 03:09.625
Follow your heart.

03:09.659 --> 03:10.626
Shut up, Butch.

03:10.659 --> 03:11.737
You're the loser of this crew.

03:11.761 --> 03:12.762
Hey guys, you hear that?

03:12.795 --> 03:14.696
Butch told me to follow my heart.

03:21.937 --> 03:25.107
Dad, can I have 50 bucks
for a shamrock tattoo?

03:25.141 --> 03:26.242
It's time.

03:26.274 --> 03:27.552
All right, but make sure you get it

03:27.576 --> 03:28.645
where everyone can see.

03:28.677 --> 03:29.645
Hold on, Peter.

03:29.678 --> 03:31.580
I-if Chris wants money for something,

03:31.613 --> 03:33.783
maybe it's time he got a part-time job.

03:33.815 --> 03:35.884
He could mow lawns or-or babysit.

03:35.917 --> 03:36.885
I can't work.

03:36.919 --> 03:37.886
I'm too young.

03:37.920 --> 03:39.221
Well, Will Smith's little kid

03:39.255 --> 03:40.423
works as a movie star,

03:40.456 --> 03:42.134
even though he looks
like a wet baby horse.

03:42.158 --> 03:44.459
All right, I suppose I could get a job.

03:44.493 --> 03:46.296
Well, maybe even my old job as the guy

03:46.328 --> 03:47.563
racing through an airport

03:47.595 --> 03:49.432
at the end of a romantic comedy.

03:50.433 --> 03:52.334
Taxi! Taxi!

03:53.535 --> 03:55.170
Hey. Are you crazy?

03:55.203 --> 03:56.806
Crazy for love.

03:56.838 --> 03:58.574
The most amazing girl I've ever met

03:58.606 --> 04:00.443
leaves on a plane in five minutes.

04:00.476 --> 04:01.711
Get in.

04:14.657 --> 04:16.358
What the hell's going on?

04:16.392 --> 04:17.659
This guy's in love.

04:17.693 --> 04:18.661
Is she worth it?

04:18.693 --> 04:21.029
She's a once-in-a-life-time girl.

04:21.063 --> 04:22.632
I'll give you an escort.

04:28.570 --> 04:30.016
No charge.

04:32.007 --> 04:34.277
Final boarding call for Ashley's flight

04:34.310 --> 04:36.846
to stuffy New England college.
Final boarding.

04:36.878 --> 04:38.780
Ooh, whoa, whoa, whoa, child.

04:38.813 --> 04:40.148
What's the hurry?

04:40.181 --> 04:42.217
The love of my life, that's what.

04:42.250 --> 04:44.152
We got a code Romeo.

04:44.185 --> 04:46.856
Repeat, code Romeo.

04:46.889 --> 04:48.624
If you get there on time,

04:48.657 --> 04:50.493
there's an extra 50 in it for you.

04:50.525 --> 04:52.494
I love this job!

04:56.866 --> 04:58.735
Ashley, wait!

05:00.935 --> 05:04.673
I wouldn't miss this for all
the rush hour fares in Bigtown.

05:04.707 --> 05:07.409
Chris, you came. Oh, my God!

05:07.443 --> 05:09.445
Let me get my grandma.

05:11.546 --> 05:12.647
Chris?

05:12.681 --> 05:15.051
Ashley. I love you.

05:20.623 --> 05:22.592
Oh, you're groaning at me?

05:22.625 --> 05:25.395
You paid $19 to fly Spirit Air.

05:25.428 --> 05:27.596
You get what you get.

05:31.534 --> 05:33.503
All right, Brian,
I've written a few songs,

05:33.536 --> 05:36.038
all about stuff babies
actually care about.

05:36.070 --> 05:37.739
No more rainbows and unicorns.

05:37.772 --> 05:39.174
Real baby issues.

05:39.207 --> 05:40.743
Right, like heartworm and parvo?

05:40.775 --> 05:42.010
No, baby stuff.

05:42.044 --> 05:43.512
Oh, oh, human babies.

05:43.546 --> 05:45.782
I didn't... I didn't realize
there was an agenda.

05:45.815 --> 05:47.582
Okay, look, just pay attention.

05:47.616 --> 05:50.419
♪ Momma liked to party
when you were in her belly ♪

05:50.452 --> 05:52.455
♪ Drinking, she did some ♪

05:52.488 --> 05:54.857
♪ Momma liked to party
when you were in her belly ♪

05:54.890 --> 05:57.226
♪ That's why you are dumb. ♪

05:57.258 --> 06:00.729
I call that "Momma Liked to Party".

06:00.762 --> 06:02.632
Stewie, that's good.
Hey, can I write one?

06:02.664 --> 06:04.299
Yeah, we need as many as we can.

06:04.332 --> 06:06.635
Our first gig is Saturday.
It's a birthday party.

06:06.669 --> 06:07.904
Wow, already?

06:07.936 --> 06:09.438
How'd you book a gig so fast?

06:09.471 --> 06:11.106
Easy. I figured out the perfect way

06:11.140 --> 06:13.575
to get the word out
to middle-aged moms.

06:14.909 --> 06:17.046
Musical entertainment,
available for parties.

06:17.079 --> 06:20.049
Musical entertainment,
available for parties.

06:20.082 --> 06:22.851
Hey. Where you drinking that Chardonnay?

06:28.022 --> 06:29.724
Oh, hey, Chris,
how's the job hunt going?

06:29.757 --> 06:32.294
Terrible. I can't find a job anywhere.

06:32.327 --> 06:34.162
A lot of people seem to be turned off

06:34.195 --> 06:35.832
by my dishonorable discharge.

06:35.865 --> 06:37.066
What, from the Army?

06:37.099 --> 06:38.301
No, it's a euphemism.

06:38.334 --> 06:39.601
Oh, yucky.

06:39.635 --> 06:42.137
Uh, you guys, I need help
unloading the groceries.

06:42.171 --> 06:45.474
My undiagnosed mom injury is flaring up.

06:46.942 --> 06:48.611
These little things of applesauce

06:48.644 --> 06:50.580
better not be for desserts.

06:50.613 --> 06:52.615
Go to hell, Glenn Quagmire!

06:52.647 --> 06:54.983
I'm sorry, but Mondays are Asian only.

06:55.017 --> 06:56.419
Why is your last name Wong?

06:56.452 --> 06:58.187
It's my married name.

06:58.219 --> 07:00.322
Now I see why you're here.

07:01.322 --> 07:02.692
Geez, what was that about?

07:02.724 --> 07:04.125
Ah, a little scheduling mix-up.

07:04.159 --> 07:06.295
I am just so busy,
I-I don't have any time

07:06.327 --> 07:08.164
to organize my own life.

07:08.197 --> 07:09.765
Wait a minute, what if you had someone

07:09.798 --> 07:12.268
to help keep you organized?
Chris is looking for work.

07:12.301 --> 07:14.135
Maybe he can help you
out, be your assistant.

07:14.169 --> 07:15.337
Huh, maybe.

07:15.370 --> 07:16.772
You have any references?

07:16.805 --> 07:19.675
Uh, "cowabunga," "schwing,"
"yada, yada, yada."

07:19.707 --> 07:21.142
Those are pretty good references.

07:21.176 --> 07:22.678
You're hired.

07:25.714 --> 07:27.350
Look at that. Look at the cake.

07:27.382 --> 07:30.019
"Happy Birthday Charlie
and Uncle Craig."

07:30.051 --> 07:32.787
And Uncle Craig's written
in a different color.

07:32.820 --> 07:34.657
Oh, poor Uncle Craig.

07:34.690 --> 07:36.959
Hey, is that your
ex-girlfriend, Olivia?

07:36.991 --> 07:38.326
God, what's she doing here?

07:38.359 --> 07:39.995
She was always such a nightmare.

07:42.865 --> 07:44.800
Olivia?! Oh, my God, do I look okay?

07:44.832 --> 07:46.969
I hate this shirt.
Switch shirts. Switch shirts!

07:47.002 --> 07:49.839
Stewie? Oh, I thought that was you.

07:49.871 --> 07:52.407
Hey, Olivia, hey, what brings you here?

07:52.440 --> 07:54.142
Oh, the birthday boy and I met

07:54.176 --> 07:56.979
at Burt Reynolds' acting
camp in Jupiter, Florida.

07:57.012 --> 07:58.748
Well, I'm glad to hear
you're still acting.

07:58.781 --> 08:01.384
You know, the last time
I saw you, you were...

08:01.416 --> 08:02.274
Burning in a cardboard house?

08:02.298 --> 08:03.661
Yeah, burning in a cardboard
house, yeah.

08:03.685 --> 08:05.596
Uh, hey, listen, uh, I don't
know if you've heard,

08:05.620 --> 08:07.322
but we're the entertainment.

08:07.356 --> 08:10.392
Aw, that's good. Good for you.

08:10.426 --> 08:12.161
Okay, great to see you.

08:12.193 --> 08:13.662
Come on, Stewie, it's not about her.

08:13.695 --> 08:16.332
It's about those six
children watching and the spazzy kid

08:16.365 --> 08:17.609
who's just waiting for the snakes.

08:17.633 --> 08:19.736
Bring out the snakes!

08:22.071 --> 08:24.840
It's a hot crowd, have fun out there.

08:24.872 --> 08:27.509
I'm gonna go feed everything
in my van to each other.

08:27.543 --> 08:29.845
Okay, kids, if
everyone's done washing their hands

08:29.877 --> 08:32.213
from the snakes, we
have some fun music for y...

08:32.246 --> 08:34.250
No climbing on the boat!

08:34.283 --> 08:37.287
Okay, now please welcome
Red Shirt Blue Shirt.

08:39.087 --> 08:40.755
All right, we're Red Shirt Blue Shirt,

08:40.789 --> 08:43.693
and here's a song we call
"Mommy and Daddy's Room."

08:43.726 --> 08:45.827
And we think it's one
you can all relate to.

08:47.663 --> 08:49.798
♪ When everybody's gone to sleep ♪

08:49.832 --> 08:51.801
♪ And you've said good night moon ♪

08:51.833 --> 08:53.635
♪ There's plenty of
noise still coming ♪

08:53.669 --> 08:55.638
♪ From Mommy and Daddy's room ♪

08:55.670 --> 08:58.073
♪ Oh, Daddy says "please,"
Mommy says "no" ♪

08:58.106 --> 09:00.375
♪ Daddy says "come
on," Mommy says "whoa" ♪

09:00.409 --> 09:02.477
♪ Daddy goes... , Mommy goes "ow" ♪

09:02.510 --> 09:04.779
♪ Daddy says "I'm
done," Mommy goes "wow" ♪

09:04.813 --> 09:06.582
♪ Daddy rolls over
and falls asleep ♪

09:06.615 --> 09:08.818
♪ Mommy drinks wine in the dark. ♪

09:13.355 --> 09:16.225
My God, did you hear 'em,
Stewie? We're a hit.

09:16.258 --> 09:17.827
We got to go out and celebrate.

09:17.860 --> 09:19.428
Oh, he can't go out with you tonight.

09:19.461 --> 09:20.763
He's got a date with me.

09:20.795 --> 09:22.397
Really? Awesome.

09:22.430 --> 09:24.299
Brian, I can't go. I'm not feeling well.

09:24.332 --> 09:25.809
Stewie, I've been
standing here the whole time.

09:25.833 --> 09:27.345
But, you know-you know
what, that's fine.

09:27.369 --> 09:30.406
I'll just go have a dog-style
celebration by myself.

09:30.438 --> 09:32.073
Yeah!

09:32.106 --> 09:33.608
Awesome time!

09:33.641 --> 09:35.477
This is very fun for me!

09:35.510 --> 09:36.611
- Hey!
- Oh, hey!

09:36.645 --> 09:39.136
- This is fun, right?
- The best!

09:39.305 --> 09:40.510
And me, too!

09:45.596 --> 09:47.432
Great crowd, babe.

09:47.465 --> 09:48.834
What are... What is this?

09:48.867 --> 09:51.137
Oh, Olivia's president of our fan club.

09:51.170 --> 09:52.838
She's also doing half the band.

09:52.870 --> 09:54.306
Do you even know what that means?

09:54.339 --> 09:56.908
Uh, let's just say I couldn't
toddle right for a week.

09:56.941 --> 09:58.176
Okay, you don't.

09:58.210 --> 09:59.450
All right, if you'll excuse me,

09:59.478 --> 10:00.979
I have a poo poo diaper.

10:02.348 --> 10:04.291
You really think this
Olivia thing is a good idea?

10:04.315 --> 10:05.283
Why wouldn't it be?

10:05.316 --> 10:06.527
I don't know. It just seems like

10:06.551 --> 10:08.454
it always ends badly for you two.

10:08.487 --> 10:10.589
And it can be tricky working with an ex.

10:10.622 --> 10:12.491
Look at Kermit and Miss Piggy.

10:12.523 --> 10:13.825
How are you feeling, Miss Piggy?

10:13.859 --> 10:15.269
I heard you called in sick yesterday.

10:15.293 --> 10:17.362
Yeah, I had a frog in my throat.

10:17.396 --> 10:18.798
Right, Kermie?

10:18.830 --> 10:20.166
Eh? Right?

10:20.199 --> 10:22.335
Please stop drinking.

10:26.372 --> 10:28.940
Okay, Chris, I think you're
gonna be a great assistant.

10:28.974 --> 10:30.484
Your paperwork appears to be in order,

10:30.508 --> 10:31.853
but before we get started, do you own

10:31.877 --> 10:33.813
a pair of rubber boots
that you'd have to wear

10:33.845 --> 10:35.147
if you worked on a fishing boat?

10:35.180 --> 10:36.382
Uh, no, I don't think so.

10:36.415 --> 10:38.484
All right, I guess
it'll be a light day today,

10:38.517 --> 10:39.828
but tomorrow you
should come wearing those.

10:39.852 --> 10:41.053
Okay, got it.

10:41.085 --> 10:43.188
Now, the first thing I need
you to do every morning

10:43.221 --> 10:45.857
is punch me in the stomach
because I'm a bad person.

10:45.891 --> 10:47.660
Is this a trick?

10:47.692 --> 10:49.627
It's the furthest thing
from a trick. Go ahead.

10:49.661 --> 10:50.963
And it should be pretty hard,

10:50.995 --> 10:53.198
I'm a worse person than you think.

10:53.232 --> 10:55.000
Okay, that's really good.

10:55.032 --> 10:58.570
Now I need you to call
Time Warner about my cable bill.

11:01.607 --> 11:04.243
All right, this one is for
all the mommies out there.

11:04.276 --> 11:07.179
This is what we're
really saying when we're crying.

11:07.211 --> 11:10.383
♪ Please put some
butt paste on my button ♪

11:10.416 --> 11:12.417
♪ Butt paste on my button ♪

11:12.450 --> 11:15.687
♪ Smear it on my button
for the fire down below ♪

11:15.720 --> 11:18.423
♪ Oh, oh, oh, butt
paste on my button ♪

11:18.456 --> 11:19.758
♪ Butt paste on my button ♪

11:19.791 --> 11:21.594
♪ Need it on my button 'cause it ♪

11:21.627 --> 11:23.596
♪ Cools and quells me so. ♪

11:26.864 --> 11:29.435
♪ Stay away, stay away ♪

11:29.468 --> 11:32.472
♪ From the big kid
in the baby swing. ♪

11:35.641 --> 11:37.610
♪ There's a little metal box ♪

11:37.642 --> 11:39.512
♪ At the top of the stairs ♪

11:39.545 --> 11:41.914
♪ In the back of the closet ♪

11:41.946 --> 11:43.916
♪ And a tiny little key ♪

11:43.949 --> 11:45.918
♪ That's hidden in a book ♪

11:45.950 --> 11:47.753
♪ In the drawer with the socks ♪

11:47.786 --> 11:50.256
♪ And I know how to use it ♪

11:50.288 --> 11:53.359
♪ To open up the box ♪

11:53.392 --> 11:56.496
♪ And that's where the gun is. ♪

12:00.065 --> 12:01.267
♪ ♪

12:01.300 --> 12:04.236
You know, I talk a lot of smack,
but at the end of the day,

12:04.268 --> 12:05.370
these guys are pros.

12:05.403 --> 12:09.207
Even Broken Arm Coyote with Washboard.

12:09.240 --> 12:10.285
Hey, let's keep this party rolling.

12:10.309 --> 12:11.911
I'll go get us another badly-scratched

12:11.944 --> 12:14.647
plastic pitcher of soda.

12:14.680 --> 12:17.248
Ugh, finally, he's doing
something useful.

12:17.282 --> 12:18.617
What? What do you mean?

12:18.650 --> 12:20.953
Nothing. It's just,
you write all the songs,

12:20.985 --> 12:23.655
you've got a better
voice, you've got the sweet bod...

12:23.689 --> 12:26.158
Oh, my God, babe.

12:26.190 --> 12:29.228
Plus, you've got all the cool
catchphrases like "damn you all"

12:29.261 --> 12:31.464
or "what the dude" or whatever.

12:31.497 --> 12:32.574
Uh, it-it's "deuce." But, uh,

12:32.598 --> 12:34.274
but yeah, you're-you're
right, it... I-I do.

